\n\\nYou've been optimising for the next correct step for so long that you've lost the thread of who was doing the optimising.\\n\\nThat's not a career problem. It's not a confidence problem. It's not something therapy fixes or a strengths assessment names.\\n\\nIt's an identity problem. And it's invisible from the outside because everything looks exactly right.\\n\\n[INSERT_EVENT_NAME] is built specifically for that moment — the mid-sentence stop. The quiet realisation that you've been answering a question nobody asked you.\\n\\nThis is what [INSERT_HOST_NAME] will start to unpick with you.\",\n    \"cta\": \"Secure your place at [INSERT_EVENT_NAME]\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — If that scenario felt uncomfortably familiar, you're already further along than you think. That recognition matters. Bring it with you.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 3,\n    \"subject\": \"Therapy didn't fix it. Here's why.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"It wasn't designed to. This problem has a different shape entirely.\",\n    \"body\": \"Here's the counterintuitive truth most high-achieving women never hear:\\n\\nYou're not broken. There's nothing to heal.\\n\\nThe identity you've been living inside wasn't forced on you. You built it — piece by piece — because it worked. It got results. It earned respect. It protected you.\\n\\nTherapy looks for wounds. This isn't a wound.\\n\\nSelf-help frameworks give you a category. But you're already an expert at adopting categories. You can read an Enneagram result and immediately know how to perform it.\\n\\nThe real problem is this: you've spent so long adapting to what each room requires that you can no longer tell a genuine preference from a conditioned one.\\n\\nThat's not a mindset problem. It's an architectural one.\\n\\nWhat [INSERT_HOST_NAME] does at [INSERT_EVENT_NAME] is not assessment. It's elimination — a forensic process that works backwards through the roles, relationships, and survival strategies layered over who you actually are.\\n\\nThe outcome isn't a new label. It's a legible account of who you are when you're not performing.\\n\\nThat's what this event begins to show you.\",\n    \"cta\": \"Claim your place at [INSERT_EVENT_NAME]\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — Most women say this is the first explanation they've heard that actually matches what their problem feels like. See if it matches yours.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 4,\n    \"subject\": \"You'll leave with something you didn't expect.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"Not a plan. Not a framework. Something more useful than either.\",\n    \"body\": \"Most events send you home with notes you never open again.\\n\\n[INSERT_EVENT_NAME] is designed to give you something specific instead.\\n\\nYou'll leave knowing how to tell the difference between a decision that's yours and one you've been carrying for someone else.\\n\\nThat sounds subtle. It isn't.\\n\\nWomen who've done this work describe the same shift: they stop saying \"I don't know what I want\" and start being able to say \"that's not mine to want.\"\\n\\nThose are very different sentences. The second one changes how you move through every room — a board meeting, a difficult conversation with your partner, a choice about what comes next professionally.\\n\\nYou also won't have to explain yourself defensively anymore. When you know what you actually think, you can say it without bracing for impact.\\n\\nThat's the benefit most women don't expect. They come looking for clarity about the future.\\n\\nThey leave with something more foundational: a stable sense of who's doing the deciding.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME] will show you exactly how that works at [INSERT_EVENT_NAME].\",\n    \"cta\": \"Join [INSERT_EVENT_NAME] and show up live\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — This particular benefit doesn't come through in a replay. It's the kind of shift that happens in a room, not from a recording. More on that tomorrow.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 5,\n    \"subject\": \"No replay for this part.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"What happens live at [INSERT_EVENT_NAME] won't be in the recording. This is the part that matters.\",\n    \"body\": \"There's a moment at [INSERT_EVENT_NAME] that [INSERT_HOST_NAME] doesn't record.\\n\\nIt's the part where the room gets quiet — because something lands that's never been said out loud before.\\n\\nYou can't get that from a replay. A replay shows you the content. It doesn't give you the moment.\\n\\nIf you've been planning to catch the recording later, I want you to think about that decision carefully.\\n\\n\"Later\" is exactly the pattern this work is designed to interrupt.\\n\\nHow many times have you said \"I'll deal with that when things settle down\" — and things have not settled down, because they won't, because that was never the real reason?\\n\\nShowing up live to [INSERT_EVENT_NAME] is a small act in the right direction. It's choosing, once, to put the thing that matters ahead of the thing that's merely urgent.\\n\\nEnrolment for the 12-week programme opens at the event. Places are limited per cohort. The women in the room get first access.\\n\\nThis is the last email before [INSERT_EVENT_NAME]. Show up.\",\n    \"cta\": \"Confirm your live attendance at [INSERT_EVENT_NAME]\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — Enrolment opens to live attendees first. If the programme is full by the time the replay goes out, the replay audience won't be able to join. Don't find that out the hard way.\"\n  }\n]"}
