[emailSequences] RETRY EXHAUST — FULL RAW CONTENT (from invokeLLM, post tool-use stringify): {"emails":"[\n  {\n    \"day\": -7,\n    \"subject\": \"They called it \"presence.\"\",\n    \"previewText\": \"You've outperformed that room for years. Something I've been building is almost ready — and it starts with that word.\",\n    \"body\": \"You've heard it before.\\n\\n\"Presence.\" \"Authority.\" \"She doesn't fill the room.\"\\n\\nNot once did they say your work wasn't excellent. Not once did they question your track record.\\n\\nThey questioned something they couldn't quite name — and handed the role to someone louder.\\n\\nI've been working on something for a while now. Something built specifically for women at your level who are tired of being told the answer is to be more.\\n\\nMore visible. More vocal. More something you're not.\\n\\nWhat I've been building starts from a different premise entirely.\\n\\nThe feedback isn't about your voice. It never was.\\n\\nI'm not ready to share everything yet. But I wanted you to know it's coming — because the women this is designed for rarely go looking for help. They recalibrate. They absorb it. They move on.\\n\\nUntil the day they stop mid-sentence and realise they don't know what they're moving toward.\\n\\nIf that sentence landed somewhere specific in your chest, keep an eye on your inbox.\\n\\nThe next email lands in a few days. It will change how you see the feedback entirely.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Watch for the next email — it arrives in a few days.\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — The thing I'm about to share has nothing to do with speaking louder, projecting more, or performing differently. That's what makes it worth waiting for.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": -4,\n    \"subject\": \"Your voice isn't the problem.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"The \"presence\" feedback is pointing at something real — but everyone's been diagnosing the wrong thing.\",\n    \"body\": \"Here's the counterintuitive thing about \"presence\" feedback:\\n\\nIt has almost nothing to do with how you sound.\\n\\nMost voice coaches will tell you to slow down, lower your register, pause more. And those techniques can help — on a good day, in a low-stakes room.\\n\\nBut here's what actually happens under pressure:\\n\\nYour voice goes thin. Your sentences get shorter. You start editing yourself in real time.\\n\\nNot because your vocal technique is wrong. Because you're not sure, in that moment, who's speaking.\\n\\nThis is the part nobody says out loud.\\n\\nWhen you've spent years adapting your personality to fit what each room requires — the board, the MD, the partner who needs reassurance — you get very good at reading what people need from you.\\n\\nSo good that you do it automatically. Before you've said a word.\\n\\nThe voice thinning is a symptom. The cause is that you've been performing authority rather than speaking from it.\\n\\nThere is a difference. And the difference is detectable, even when the words are exactly right.\\n\\nThis is the principle everything I've been building rests on.\\n\\nDoes this match what you've noticed — in yourself, or in the rooms you sit in?\\n\\nHit reply. I read every response.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Hit reply and tell me — does this match your experience?\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — In 48 hours I'm sharing a specific method for getting back to the voice that was yours before the adapting started. You'll want to see this one.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": -2,\n    \"subject\": \"What actually happens in week one.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"Not a theory. A specific process — and what it produces before the end of the first month.\",\n    \"body\": \"Let me show you what this method actually does — not in principle, but in practice.\\n\\nWeek one doesn't start with assessment. It doesn't begin with a quiz or a framework or a label.\\n\\nIt begins with elimination.\\n\\nSpecifically: a forensic walk through every role you currently perform. The Commercial Director. The partner. The competent one. The measured one.\\n\\nFor each role, one question: which traits showed up because of genuine preference — and which showed up because they worked?\\n\\nThat distinction sounds simple. It is not simple.\\n\\nMost women at this level have been rewarded for adaptability for so long that they've lost the ability to tell the difference between a real preference and a conditioned one.\\n\\nThe process makes that distinction visible. Systematically. Across contexts. Over time — not in a single self-report session.\\n\\nBy the end of the first four weeks, most women can name at least three core values that belong to them — not to their profession, their role, or their social group.\\n\\nThat's the stable internal reference point that changes how authority sounds.\\n\\nNot a technique. Not a performance adjustment. A legible account of who you actually are.\\n\\nThe doors open on [INSERT_CART_OPEN_DATE].\\n\\nI'll send everything you need to know then.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Watch for the cart-open email on [INSERT_CART_OPEN_DATE].\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — The programme is limited to [INSERT_COHORT_LIMIT] places. If you've been reading these emails and something has been landing, you'll want to be ready to move.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 0,\n    \"subject\": \"It's live.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"Everything you need to know about [INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME] — what's included, what it costs, and how to claim your place.\",\n    \"body\": \"[INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME] is open for enrolment right now.\\n\\nHere's exactly what's included:\\n\\nA [INSERT_PROGRAMME_DURATION] 1:1 coaching programme. Built for senior women — VP level and above — who have been told they lack \"presence\" or \"authority\" and know that performing louder is not the answer.\\n\\nThe method works through elimination, not assessment. We identify what's yours — your actual voice, your genuine preferences, your stable internal reference — by systematically removing what isn't.\\n\\nWhat you leave with:\\n\\nA clear, private identity map that separates who you are from the roles you perform. The ability to speak from authority under pressure — in a board room, in a difficult conversation, in any room that needs something from you. Honest conversations with managers, partners, or teams that don't collapse into self-erasure or over-explaining.\\n\\nWhat it costs: [INSERT_PRICE]\\n\\nWhat protects your investment: [INSERT_GUARANTEE_TERMS]\\n\\nPlaces are limited to [INSERT_COHORT_LIMIT] women per cohort.\\n\\nCart closes on [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_DATE] at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME].\\n\\nIf you've been waiting for the right moment — the one where you actually know what you're recalibrating toward — this is it.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Enrol in [INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME] now and claim your place.\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — If you have a question before enrolling, hit reply. I answer personally. But do it today — the cohort fills and I can't hold places.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 1,\n    \"subject\": \"If you've been \"too measured\"…\",\n    \"previewText\": \"This is specifically for the woman who gets told she's considered, careful, and not quite right for the role.\",\n    \"body\": \"If you're a Commercial Director, a VP, a Head of something — and the feedback keeps coming back as \"measured,\" \"considered,\" or \"not quite the presence we need\" — this email is specifically for you.\\n\\nYou didn't get that feedback because you're wrong.\\n\\nYou got it because you're very good at reading rooms. And somewhere along the way, reading rooms became your default — even in the rooms where you should be the one setting the tone.\\n\\nHere's what that looks like in practice:\\n\\nYou walk into a board meeting with a clear position. The first pushback comes. You hear yourself soften it — not because the pushback was right, but because the room needed something from you and you gave it automatically.\\n\\nYour voice didn't go thin because you lack authority. It went thin because you couldn't locate yourself fast enough to hold the position.\\n\\n[INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME] is built for exactly this.\\n\\nThe [INSERT_PROGRAMME_DURATION] process gives you a stable internal reference point — something to speak from rather than perform toward.\\n\\nBy week eight, most women in this programme can sit in a room full of demands without automatically reshaping to fit what's required.\\n\\nThat shift is audible. Measurably, observably audible.\\n\\nThe cart is open now. [INSERT_COHORT_LIMIT] places per cohort.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Enrol now and secure your place in the current cohort.\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — The cart closes on [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_DATE] at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME]. If \"measured\" has followed you through more than one performance review, this cohort is the one to be in.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 3,\n    \"subject\": \"The real reason you haven't enrolled.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"It's not the price. It's not the timing. Here's what's actually sitting in the way.\",\n    \"body\": \"Let me name what's actually happening.\\n\\nYou've read the emails. Something has landed. But you haven't enrolled — and you're telling yourself it's because you need to think about it.\\n\\nHere's what \"I need to think about it\" usually means at your level:\\n\\nIt means: \"I'm not sure I'm the kind of person who does this sort of thing.\"\\n\\nBecause you've already tried therapy. And the frameworks. And the self-help books that told you to find your why.\\n\\nNone of it solved this — because none of it was designed for this.\\n\\nTherapy is oriented around healing. This isn't a wound — it's an architectural problem. The identity you're performing was built deliberately, piece by piece, in response to real incentives. There is nothing to heal. There is something to reconstruct.\\n\\nFrameworks returned a category. You're already expert at adopting categories. That's not what's missing.\\n\\nWhat's missing is a forensic process applied to your actual biographical material — not a personality type, not a label, not a reflection exercise.\\n\\nIf none of the above has worked, it's not because you didn't try hard enough. It's because you were using the wrong tools.\\n\\n[INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME] is a different tool entirely.\\n\\nIf after reading this it still doesn't feel like a fit — that's genuinely okay. But if the real reason is hesitation, not mismatch, that's worth sitting with.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Enrol now if this is the tool you've been missing.\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — The guarantee is [INSERT_GUARANTEE_TERMS]. The risk of trying a different tool is lower than you think.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 5,\n    \"subject\": \"I almost forgot to mention this.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"There's a bonus I haven't told you about yet. Here's what it is — and what it specifically gives you.\",\n    \"body\": \"I should have mentioned this when the cart opened.\\n\\nEveryone who enrols in [INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME] before [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_DATE] receives an unannounced bonus — valued at [INSERT_BONUS_VALUE].\\n\\nHere's what it is:\\n\\nA private, pre-programme intensive session with [INSERT_HOST_NAME] before the [INSERT_PROGRAMME_DURATION] work begins.\\n\\nThe sole purpose of that session: map the specific rooms and relationships where your voice goes thin under pressure — so week one of the programme isn't spent identifying the problem. It's spent solving it.\\n\\nMost women arrive knowing something is wrong. Fewer can name which exact contexts collapse their authority and why.\\n\\nThis session gives you that map before we start. It compresses the timeline. It means the work we do in the first four weeks is targeted rather than exploratory.\\n\\nValued at [INSERT_BONUS_VALUE]. Included at no extra cost for this cohort only.\\n\\nThe total package — [INSERT_PROGRAMME_DURATION] of 1:1 work, the identity map, the method, plus this intensive — is [INSERT_PRICE].\\n\\nThe cart closes [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_DATE] at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME].\\n\\nPlaces remaining: [INSERT_COHORT_LIMIT] maximum per cohort.\\n\\nIf this bonus makes the decision clearer, now is the moment.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Enrol now to claim the bonus before the cart closes.\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — This bonus is not available after [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_DATE]. It's specific to this cohort and will not be carried forward.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 7,\n    \"subject\": \"What closes tonight.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"Cart closes [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_DATE] at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME]. Here's exactly what you lose access to after that.\",\n    \"body\": \"The cart for [INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME] closes today — [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_DATE] at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME].\\n\\nAfter that point, enrolment is closed. The cohort will be full or the window will have passed.\\n\\nHere's what closes with it:\\n\\nThe pre-programme intensive session — valued at [INSERT_BONUS_VALUE] — available to this cohort only.\\n\\nThe current price of [INSERT_PRICE]. Pricing for future cohorts is not confirmed.\\n\\nYour place in a cohort limited to [INSERT_COHORT_LIMIT] women. The next opportunity to enrol is no earlier than [INSERT_COHORT_CLOSE_DATE].\\n\\nThis is the programme for women who've been told they don't fill the room — and are done absorbing that feedback and recalibrating toward something they haven't chosen.\\n\\nThe [INSERT_PROGRAMME_DURATION] process doesn't ask you to perform authority. It helps you locate the voice you already have — the one that was yours before the adapting started.\\n\\nIf you've been waiting for a sign that this is the right moment: the cart closing tonight is the most concrete sign available.\\n\\nEnrol before [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME] today.\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Enrol now before the cart closes at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME].\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — If you have one question standing between you and enrolling, hit reply right now. I'm at my desk and I'll respond before the cart closes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 7,\n    \"subject\": \"Last hours. One question answered.\",\n    \"previewText\": \"You've been wondering if this will actually work for someone at your level. Here's the honest answer.\",\n    \"body\": \"You've been wondering something.\\n\\nNot whether the programme sounds right — it does, or you'd have stopped reading these emails days ago.\\n\\nYou've been wondering: \"Will it actually work for someone like me?\"\\n\\nSomeone who's already done the therapy. Already read the books. Already tried the frameworks and found they returned a category she immediately knew how to perform.\\n\\nHere's the honest answer:\\n\\nThis process was built for exactly that woman. Not for someone earlier in her career who is still forming her identity. For someone who has a fully formed, highly functional identity that no longer belongs to her.\\n\\nThe elimination process works because it doesn't ask you to discover who you are. It asks you to notice who you aren't — and it does that systematically, across the actual contexts of your actual life, over [INSERT_PROGRAMME_DURATION].\\n\\nThat's a different question. And it's one you haven't been asked before.\\n\\nThis is the last email about [INSERT_LAUNCH_PRODUCT_NAME].\\n\\nThe cart closes at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME] today.\\n\\nIf you enrol: you start the process of speaking from a stable self rather than performing toward one.\\n\\nIf you don't: the next performance review will use the same word. And you'll absorb it again.\\n\\nThe choice is yours. But the window closes at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME].\\n\\n[INSERT_HOST_NAME]\",\n    \"cta\": \"Enrol now — the cart closes at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME] today.\",\n    \"ps\": \"PS — This is genuinely the last email. The cart closes at [INSERT_CART_CLOSE_TIME] and I won't be reopening it. If you're in, now is the moment.\"\n  }\n]"}
